            "width": 1920
          }
        ],
        "name": "DogeDesigner",
        "text": "Elon Musk in his new interview on “suicidal empathy”\n\n“I think you don’t want to have misguided empathy. I agree with Gad Saad’s philosophy here. And suicidal empathy is, you know, that’s his term. You ideally want people to be default trusted, not default distrusted. And you want to encourage behavior that is good for society, you know, for people to do good things that are good for their fellow human beings. And ultimately, that actually does end up being good for the individual, provided it is mutual. So if you think everyone is like yourself, then you’re going to have a problem, because this is simply not true. There are peoples and cultures with very different views.”",
        "url": "https://x.com/cb_doge/status/2112573201285030230",
