        "name": "World of Statistics",
        "text": "🌍 European countries that added the most migrants (2000–2024)\n\n1. 🇬🇧 United Kingdom: +7.1M\n2. 🇪🇸 Spain: +6.8M\n3. 🇩🇪 Germany: +6.4M\n4. 🇹🇷 Türkiye: +5.8M\n5. 🇮🇹 Italy: +4.4M\n6. 🇫🇷 France: +3.0M\n7. 🇦🇹 Austria: +1.4M\n8. 🇳🇱 Netherlands: +1.4M\n9. 🇨🇭 Switzerland: +1.3M\n10. 🇧🇪 Belgium: +1.3M\n11. 🇸🇪 Sweden: +1.3M\n12. 🇵🇱 Poland: +917K\n13. 🇮🇪 Ireland: +840K\n14. 🇳🇴 Norway: +720K\n15. 🇷🇴 Romania: +521K\n16. 🇵🇹 Portugal: +476K\n17. 🇩🇰 Denmark: +475K\n18. 🇭🇺 Hungary: +393K\n19. 🇨🇿 Czechia: +386K\n20. 🇫🇮 Finland: +378K\n\nEurope's migrant population grew by 40.8 million between 2000 and 2024, up 67%. The UK, Spain and Germany together account for almost half of that increase.\n\nSource: UN DESA",
